    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Vickers Viscount 745-\nAfter W.W. II, the relatively new pure jets were\nconsidered impractical for the short haul. In-\nstead, turbines were used to drive propellers.\nThe Vickers-Amrstrongs Viscount, flown ini-\ntially in 1948, was the first propeller-turbine\ntransport, and became the most successful Brit-\nish transport ever built. Length: 81'10\". Wing-\nspan: 93'8½\". Cruising speed: 324 mph.\nSand\nCopyright 1973 by Johns-Byrne Co., Chicago, III.\nLAX - SFO\n7-29-74\nPLACE\nSTAMP\nHERE\nНени\nSpecial Offer\nPrints of this art available 9\" × 12\", ready to frame. Send $2.00 check or money order for each print to: Johns-Byrne Co., 161 W. Harrison, Chicago, III. 60605.\nPlease specify type of aircraft (Viscount). Complete list of other available aircraft prints will be sent to you with your order. Allow three weeks for delivery."
    ],
